From 96fda857a0c2f3e8e6abb08868011a5ff7a4dd6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kierandrewett <kieran@drewett.dev>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:25:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] x11: frame managed windows from the compositor

Do not launch mutter-x11-frames and never reparent a client into a frame
window. An X11 window is framed like an xdg toplevel: the compositor's frame
actor is drawn around the client, and the layout comes from
meta_gnoblin_window_frame_x11_update. That runs when the window is created,
when its decorations hint, type or fullscreen state changes, and when it
declares _GTK_FRAME_EXTENTS, which now feed the overlay instead of
window->custom_frame_extents directly.

The initial state of a managed window is set after window-created, once the
frame layout is known. The decorated-and-not-framed gates that kept a window
unmapped until its frame existed are gone, and the input region and
configure-request width no longer depend on a frame window.
---
